Z||000009||dogtired||12-09-1999||11:55 AM||||OK, I am sure you have all suspected it, but this will show my true colors.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR>Talking about "B" movies there is a Andy Sadaris film called "L.E.A.T.H.E.L. ladies" and with some of the ladies in it, it is tough to look at the cars, almost rated X. Anyway about 1/3 of the way into the show there is a scene by an aircraft hangar, and there is a red fiero Kitcar that they get into and drive away in. Anyway I had to watch the girls, er I mean I had to watch the film about 3 times to make sure but look at the interior and the sun roof, of the car. I can't tell what year it is but no doubt it is one of ours.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> Think Ill go watch it again. Don't know if it can be rented? (get your mind out of the gutter, I am talking about the film)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/redface.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000010||turbo86se||12-10-1999||11:05 AM||||Have any of you guys seen the movie "Army of One" with Dolph Lundgren? It's a slow start, but it picks up when he steals the Ferrari F40 (clearly a Fiero) and is chased by a Lamborghini Countach (not sure). Lots of Diablo kit cars in other scenes. Not a great movie, but worth checking out. I was watching this movie late one night with my g'friend a few years ago, she sure was mad when I started paying more attention to the movie than her!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||DJRice||12-10-1999||11:18 AM||||Those Sidaris Films are something else, aren't they?  ||||reg||1
Z||000012||dogtired||12-10-1999||12:28 PM||||Fiero Spotting (but in real life)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>I went hunting yesterday, around lunch time, let me make this clear. I never go hunting with a gun or bullits or camping or boots. Usually with at least a 1/2 tank gas and sharp eyes, note pad or camera.<BR>I was driving down this sand road and up ahead I saw a BIG dog stand along the side. That wasn't unusual till I got up beside him, there was this yard with an 8foot chain link fence around it and up in front of the garage was a white 88 coupe, really sorry looking, windshield gone, tires flat, really grungy. Anyway there were 2 more BIGGER dogs, one standing on the top of the car and the other laying on the hood? What a sight? Well in my normal hunting fashon I noted the address and will go by there several more times till I see a human around that I can ask about the car. I am not afarid of dogs but I was out weighed and out numbered  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> Wish I had a digital camera, you would all have enjoyed that.||||reg||1
